  "worked_solution": "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n\u2026,\\,-24,\\,-19,\\,-14,\\,-9,\\,-4,\\,\u2026\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =5 \\\\  & =-19-(-24) \\\\  & =-14-(-19) \\\\  & =-9-(-14) \\\\  & =\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=-4,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =-4+(n-1)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-4+5n-5 \\\\  & =5n-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={5n-9\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$",
